<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dedition of Nice to Savoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1388">1388</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Dedition of Nice</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> to Savoy was the act of 1388 by which Nice and its hinterland, then part of the county of Provence, placed themselves under the protection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-vii-count-of-savoy">Amadeus VII, Count of Savoy</a>. It followed the succession war after the death of Queen Joanna I, in which Nice refused to accept Louis II of Anjou. The territory, later called the County of Nice, remained Savoyard almost continuously until 1860.</p></div>
